A||N||6||grinthock||Door Poppers||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||05-30-2001||07:15 PM||||Anyone seen a fiero or added door poppers ?  Those things that open the doors?  I know a guy here put them on his F355 conversion... What's the process?  Is it a big deal?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||05-30-2001||07:23 PM||||There not excatly in popular demand in my town, but I did install them on a Celica once. They are kinda a *****  to do, and unless someone makes a kit, will likly require some modification to the insides of the door. My solution for my Fiero was just to put an electric switch under it, that unlocks the doors when pushed. Much easier then door poppers and serves the same purpose.||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||05-30-2001||07:25 PM||||electric switch where?  Under the door handle?  I guess that would work too!  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||05-30-2001||07:59 PM||||In my kit car I had speaker wire mounted on the underside of the car that went to the power lock unit.  I didn't have handles on the outside so if the remote doors failed all I had to do was put power to the wires and it opened up the locks.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kick.gif">  <BR>THE NORTHSTAR GIVES YOU A REAL KICK IN THE ASS!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||sjp777||05-30-2001||08:35 PM||||Get an alarm with remote keyless entry.<P>Mine was only $200 installed and it unlocks the doors, turns on the interior lights, and can pop the trunk.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">    <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||05-30-2001||09:24 PM||||Basically what you do is use the door lock solonoid to open the door instead of work the lock||||reg||1
